  println("{n.abs()}")
  ```
  This prints `2.5`.
:##
public extend f64 abs() f64:
    return llvm.fabs_f64(self)

##:
Gives the smaller of the value and `b`.

- Parameter b: The other value.
- Returns: The smaller of the two values.
- Example:
  ```sushi
  let i8 n = 7
  println("{n.min(3)}")
  ```
  This prints `3`.
:##
public extend i8 min(i8 b) i8:
    if (self < b):
        return self
    return b

