##:
Gives the smaller of the value and `b`.

A NaN on one side gives the other value, as the C `fmin` does.

- Parameter b: The other value.
- Returns: The smaller of the two values.
- Example:
  ```sushi
  let f32 n = -2.5
  println("{n.min(3.0)}")
  ```
  This prints `-2.5`.
:##
public extend f32 min(f32 b) f32:
    return llvm.minnum_f32(self, b)

##:
Gives the smaller of the value and `b`.

A NaN on one side gives the other value, as the C `fmin` does.

