  println("{n.min(3.0)}")
  ```
  This prints `-2.5`.
:##
public extend f64 min(f64 b) f64:
    return llvm.minnum_f64(self, b)

##:
Gives the larger of the value and `b`.

- Parameter b: The other value.
- Returns: The larger of the two values.
- Example:
  ```sushi
